# =============================================================================
# store rule — Q-X3 (operator ruling 2026-10-15, need): the store half.
#
# `a + a` over `ti8` is a `ti16` intermediate typed by the scalar range rule, so
# 100 + 100 = 200 is carried exactly and the expression itself never traps. The
# declared element width applies once, at the store into `s`: 200 does not fit
# `i8`, so the run aborts at that declaration (`implicit_store_out_of_range`).
#
# This is the negative twin of `store-rule-midexpr.fab`: same rule, opposite
# observable — there the intermediate fits after the `/ 2`, here it does not fit
# at all. Nothing is printed; a wrapping regression would print [−56, 2] and is
# caught by the unexpected-pass ratchet.
# =============================================================================

main {
    let list<i8> flat_a ← [100, 1]
    let ti8[2] a ← flat_a ↦ ti8[2]
    let ti8[2] s ← a + a
    print s.flatten()
}
